  ],
  "description": "Black-box Mk I, common 3.3 kΩ / 4.7 kΩ input filter and 47 pF feedback capacitor. Transcribed from the General Guitar Gadgets Vintage BluesBreaker original-wiring drawing, 20 May 2019. The single 100 kΩ gain pot affects both TL072 sections. The engaged footswitch opens the interstage shunt. The 8.4 V supply represents a 9 V battery after D5; indicator and bypass contacts are omitted. TL072 output bounds are estimated. Two 100 MΩ leakage paths reference the otherwise floating series-diode midpoints.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Gain",
      "Tone",
      "Volume"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Marshall Bluesbreaker Mk I",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
